  "description": "NeuML PubMedBERT Base Embeddings is an Apache-2.0 sentence-transformers model fine-tuned from PubMedBERT for biomedical sentence and paragraph embeddings. The established TEI CUDA 1.9.3 Forge row supports B200, H200, L40S, and RTX6000 but not B300/SM103; the separate TEI 100-latest Blackwell experiment was mirrored to all regions and then failed before readiness with `Runtime compute cap 103 is not compatible with compile time compute cap 100`. This hidden manifest adds the next fallback candidate without changing either TEI row: reuse the already mirrored official vLLM 0.21.0 CUDA 13 image, launch it with `--runner pooling`, and force mean pooling with embedding activation to match the upstream sentence-transformers pooling config. Current research on 2026-05-27 confirms the Hugging Face artifact remains public, ungated, enabled, Apache-2.0 licensed, sentence-transformers based, and tagged for text-embeddings-inference. The vLLM 0.21.0 image digest is already present in all four active Forge registries, reports CUDA 13.0.2, and comes from the Apache-2.0 vllm-project/vllm repository. The hidden six-cell 3-warmup/10-run matrix passed after correcting the vLLM 0.21 PoolerConfig flags, but this row must stay onboarding/default-ineligible until full embedding parity against the TEI CUDA 1.9.3 row and healthcare product safety review are complete.",
